WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Welcome to gradient descent fundamentals.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Today we're going to explore why we subtract the gradient instead of adding it.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:25.000
This is a common point of confusion, but the answer lies in the direction of steepest descent.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:35.000
The gradient vector points in the direction of steepest ascent,
so subtracting it moves us towards the minimum.
